["I need to make 24 using 9, 5, 6, 3 with each number once.\n\nLet me try combinations.\n\n9 + 5 + 6 + 3 = 23. No.\n9 + 5 + 6 - 3 = 17. No.\n9 * 5 - 6 * 3 = 45 - 18 = 27. No.\n9 - 5 + 6 * 3 = 4 + 18 = 22. No.\n(9 - 5) * 6 = 24, then need to use 3. (9-5)*6*3 = 72. (9-5)*6/3 = 8. (9-5)*6+3 = 27. (9-5)*6-3 = 21.\n(9 - 5) * 6 = 24 but I need to use 3.\n\nLet me think.\n9 * 3 - 5 + 6 = 27 - 5 + 6 = 28. No.\n9 * 3 - 6 + 5 = 27 - 6 + 5 = 26. No.\n9 * 3 - 6 - 5 = 16. No.\n9 * 3 - 5 - 6 = 16. No.\n(9 + 3) * (6 - 5) = 12. No.\n(9 + 3) * 6 / 5 = 72/5. No.\n(9 - 3) * (6 - 5) = 6. No.\n(9 - 3) * 6 - 5 = 36 - 5 = 31. No.\n(9 - 3) * 6 / 5 = 36/5. No.\n(9 - 3) * 5 - 6 = 30 - 6 = 24! Yes!\n\nLet me verify: (9 - 3) * 5 - 6 = 6 * 5 - 6 = 30 - 6 = 24. Yes!\n\nUses 9, 3, 5, 6 each once. \n\nSo the answer is (9 - 3) * 5 - 6.\n"]